subject: [[your old clients | who's calling your past clients? | clients you already won]]

Hi {first_name|there},

(({company.opener}))

I'm a software engineering student at the University of Waterloo, so I'm chasing internships every co-op term. Hiring runs in seasons, and I'd guess you feel that more than I do.

I've built production systems with big teams at the Government of Canada (one is used by 17,000 staff) and with a small team at a University of Alberta lab. Now I'm looking to work with recruiting firms.

You've got years of past clients sitting in your ATS that nobody's called in a while. Guess what a lot of them are probably doing right now? Hiring. Just not through you.

I'll email them for you and book you {offer.goal} meetings in {offer.days} days. If I don't book one, you get every dollar back.

I know you're busy, so it's one 30-minute call at the start and an export from your ATS. I handle the rest.

I recorded a short walkthrough of how it works. Want me to send it? Or if you'd rather talk, how does {call.times} sound? I can send you a Google Meet invite, or you can name a time that suits you better. Just let me know.

William
